--How many ReplicaSets exist on the system?
	*kubectl get replicaset 
	*kubectl get rs

--How many pods are desired in the replica set?
	*kubectl get rs
		- Look for the desired tab and it will show how many pods are desired

--What is the image used to create the pods in the new-replica-set?
	*kubectl describe replicaset
	*kubectl describe rs

--How many pods are ready in the replicaset?
	*kubectl get pods 
		- Look at the ready tab when running the command
	*kubectl describe pod xyz
		- See why the pod is failing

**After deleting a pod that was created by the replicaset because there is a desired state for how many should be running a new on will be auto created 

--Create a replicaset using the replicaset-definition-1.yaml file located at /root/
	*kubectl create -f replicatset-defininion-1.yaml
	*kubectl get rs

--Fix the issue in the replicaset-definition-2.yaml
	*kubectl create -f replicaset-definiaion-2.yaml
	*kubectl get rs

--Delete two newly created replicasets replicaset-1 && replicaset-2
	*kubectl delete -f relicaset-1.yaml
	*kubectl delete -f replicaset-2.yaml

